        "title": "Communication Visionaries: McLuhan, Innis, Licklider, Negroponte",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "INNIS (1940s-1951):\n  Empires are built on their communication infrastructure.\n  Time-biased media (stone, parchment): durable; preserve\n    tradition; support decentralized power over time\n  Space-biased media (paper, radio): perishable; project\n    power over distance; support centralized empires"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-COMMUNICATION-VISIONARIES.md#004",
      "path": [
        "06-COMMUNICATION-VISIONARIES.md"
      ],
