        "title": "Communication Visionaries: McLuhan, Innis, Licklider, Negroponte",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE THROUGH-LINE:\n  Innis → McLuhan: media shapes culture (Canadian media theory)\n  Licklider → Negroponte: media should be interactive and personal\n                          (American computing tradition)\n  All four: the technology is not neutral; it has cognitive and\n            social effects that precede and exceed its content\n```"
